Q: How can I remove a specific item from an array in JavaScript? A: <p>If you are restricted to <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ExtendScript" rel="nofollow noreferrer">ExtendScript</a> as an <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_InDesign" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Adobe InDesign</a> scripter, then you could use the following function. Please keep in mind that InDesign has only ExtendScript dd. from the late 1990s incorporated where many &quot;modern&quot; JavaScript function aren't available, so the vast majority of the suggested solutions in previous answers won't work in InDesign, unfortunately.</p>
<p>Also keep in mind that really &quot;global&quot;/&quot;local&quot; variables were not part of ECMAScript at that time.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function removeItemOnce(arr, value) {
    for (i in arr) {
        if (arr[i] == value) {
            arr = arr.splice(i, 1);
            break;
    }
    }
    return arr;
}
</code></pre>
